.TH DOTTORE 1 "2026" "Il Dottore" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dottore \- spec-driven security scanner for LLMs and AI applications (nmap-for-AI)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dottore
.I run
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fITARGET\fR...] \fB--scope\fR \fIscope.yaml\fR
.br
.B dottore
.I fingerprint
\fITARGET\fR \fB--scope\fR \fIscope.yaml\fR
.br
.B dottore
.I fleet
\fIfleet.yaml\fR [\fB--run\fR] [\fB--judge\fR \fIjudge.yaml\fR]
.br
.B dottore
.I "lint | describe | registry | new-spec | replay | diff | schema"
[\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dottore
(alias
.BR dott )
examines an AI endpoint, diagnoses its security weaknesses against a declarative attack
battery aligned to the OWASP LLM Top 10, MITRE ATLAS and NIST AI 600-1, and issues a
reproducible, evidence-backed report mapped to operational risk.
.PP
It is a defensive tool. It scans nothing without a signed
.I scope.yaml
(endpoint allowlist, default-deny), never performs real destructive actions or
exfiltration (mocked tools and planted canaries), and redacts secrets and PII at rest.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Run a campaign against one or more targets (the default command).
.TP
.B fingerprint
Identify the model and guardrails behind an endpoint; attack nothing.
.TP
.B fleet
Expand a fleet.yaml into an authorization scope plus one target file per model; with
.B --run
scan them all.
.TP
.B lint
Schema, policy and fixtures-prove-detection lint of the specs.
.TP
.B describe
Show one spec's detail card.
.TP
.B registry ls
List the attack-spec catalogue (filter by --category, --owasp, --tag, --suite).
.TP
.B new-spec
Scaffold a new attack spec and empty fixtures.
.TP
.B replay
Re-read a run from stored evidence, sending nothing.
.TP
.B diff
Compare a run against a baseline and surface regressions (CI-gateable).
.TP
.B schema export
Print the JSON Schemas that validate every spec.
.SH "RUN OPTIONS"
.TP
.B --scope \fIPATH\fR
REQUIRED authorization record. Never bypassable.
.TP
.B -t, --target \fIPATH\fR
Target file(s); repeatable. Targets may also be positional.
.TP
.B --judge \fIPATH\fR
Judge model target.yaml (LLM-as-judge for the semantic_judge evaluator on live scans).
.TP
.B --suite \fITEXT\fR
Suite id or alias: owasp:llm, quick, multi-turn, access-control, agentic-owasp2026,
obfuscation-enhancers, embeddings, agentic-extortion.
.TP
.B -p, --categories \fITEXT\fR
Comma-separated categories: pi, jailbreak, leakage, tool, rag, output, dos.
.TP
.B --spec \fITEXT\fR, --exclude \fITEXT\fR
Run or skip specific spec ids or globs (e.g. PI-*); repeatable.
.TP
.B --quick, --deep
T0 minimum battery / T2 deep-agentic suite.
.TP
.B -sn, -sV, -A
Discovery only / fingerprint first / aggressive (-sV + deep + adaptive).
.TP
.B --runs \fIN\fR
Reproducibility runs (default 5).
.TP
.B -T \fI0..5\fR
Timing template (default 3); higher is faster and louder.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Resolve and validate the plan; send nothing.
.TP
.B --compare
Model-comparison matrix across targets.
.TP
.B -oJ, -oH, -oS, -oX \fIPATH\fR; -oA \fIPREFIX\fR
Write JSON / HTML / SARIF / JUnit; -oA writes all four to <prefix>.*.
.TP
.B --fail-on \fIBAND\fR
CI gate on confirmed findings: low|medium|high|critical (default high).
.TP
.B --include-needs-review
Also gate low-confidence findings.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Clean: no gated finding at or above --fail-on.
.TP
.B 1
Findings present but all below --fail-on.
.TP
.B 2
At least one gated finding at or above --fail-on.
.TP
.B 3
Operational error (bad scope, unknown suite, I/O).
.PP
Only an exploited (fail) finding trips the gate; pass and inconclusive never do.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I scope.yaml
Authorization record: version and targets (each with base_url, endpoints, identities). See
.BR dottore-scope (5).
.TP
.I target.yaml
The target: id, type, provider, endpoint, model, auth_ref, capabilities.
.TP
.I fleet.yaml
Many targets in one file; expanded by
.B dottore fleet.
.TP
.I .dottore/
Evidence store and run database (runtime artifacts; do not commit).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Quick triage, all report formats:
.PP
.RS
.B dottore run --quick -t target.yaml --scope scope.yaml -oA report
.RE
.PP
OWASP LLM Top 10, fingerprint first, gate CI on high/critical:
.PP
.RS
.B dottore run --suite owasp:llm -sV --fail-on high -t target.yaml --scope scope.yaml
.RE
.PP
Scan a local model with an LLM judge (no API key):
.PP
.RS
.B dottore run --quick -t local.yaml --judge judge.yaml --scope scope.yaml
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR dottore-scope (5)
